msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Installation and Environment Configuration\n"
"\n"
"## 1. Installation\n"
"\n"
"### 1.1 Installing the Triton-Ascend Compiler\n"
"\n"
"Triton-Ascend is an open-source compiler based on the Triton framework, supporting Ascend NPU operators. You can install it via pip:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install triton-ascend\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Alternatively, you can build and install from source:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"git clone https://github.com/Ascend/Triton-Ascend.git\n"
"cd Triton-Ascend\n"
"python setup.py install\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 1.2 Installing CANN\n"
"\n"
"Triton-Ascend relies on the CANN (Compute Architecture for Neural Networks) toolkit. Install CANN version 9.1.0 or later, and configure the environment variables:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"source /usr/local/Ascend/ascend-toolkit/set_env.sh\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## 2. Environment Configuration\n"
"\n"
"### 2.1 Configuring the Ascend NPU Environment\n"
"\n"
"Before running Triton-Ascend, ensure the Ascend NPU driver and firmware are properly installed. Verify the device status:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"npu-smi info\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 2.2 Setting Environment Variables\n"
"\n"
"Triton-Ascend supports the following environment variables for debugging and performance tuning:\n"
"\n"
"| Environment Variable | Default Value | Description |\n"
"| ------------------- | ------------- | ----------- |\n"
"| `TRITON_DEBUG` | `0` | Enables debug log output when set to `1` |\n"
"| `TRITON_INTERPRET` | `0` | Enables interpreter mode when set to `1` |\n"
"| `TRITON_ALL_BLOCKS_PARALLEL` | `0` | Enables parallel execution of all blocks when set to `1` |\n"
"| `MLIR_ENABLE_DUMP` | `0` | Enables MLIR intermediate representation dump when set to `1` |\n"
"\n"
"### 2.3 Verifying the Installation\n"
"\n"
"Run the following Python code to verify that Triton-Ascend is correctly installed:\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n"
"    block_start = pid * BLOCK_SIZE\n"
"    offsets = block_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    output = x + y\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, output, mask=mask)\n"
"\n"
"# Launch the kernel on the Ascend NPU\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If the code executes without errors, the installation is successful.\n"

msgid "安装指南"
msgstr "Installation Guide"

msgid "**Triton-Ascend**是适配华为Ascend处理器的Triton优化版本，主要用于提供高效的核函数自动调优、算子编译及部署能力，支持Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950系列产品，兼容Triton核心语法的同时，针对昇腾NPU特性进行了深度优化，包括自动解析核函数参数、优化内存访问逻辑、完善安全部署机制等。帮助用户在昇腾平台上快速开发和部署高性能计算任务。"
msgstr "**Triton-Ascend** is an optimized version of Triton adapted for Huawei Ascend processors, primarily designed to provide efficient kernel autotuning, operator compilation, and deployment capabilities. It supports Ascend Atlas A2/A3/950 series products and, while remaining compatible with core Triton syntax, has been deeply optimized for Ascend NPU features, including automatic parsing of kernel parameters, optimization of memory access logic, and enhancement of secure deployment mechanisms. It helps users rapidly develop and deploy high-performance computing tasks on the Ascend platform."

